name escort-protect-1
timeout 200

# `objective protect` — THE EXACT DUAL OF `kill`, READ THE OTHER WAY (round C12). A hostile CCIP attacker
# is inbound on a friendly ground installation; a barrier CAP has to make sure the installation is still
# there at the end of the run.
#
# READING RULE (binding): SUCCESS/exit 0 is the pass criterion, and the RESULT reason must be
# "objectives met, survived". `protect` is answered in Finalize and NEVER earlier — the thing protected
# can still be hit at t=199 — so a SUCCESS logged before the run ends would itself be the defect. What
# has to be in `events.log` is the whole causal chain: `sms RELEASE` (cap, aim120, t=20.4),
# `stores DETONATION target=striker` (t=54.3, 0.12 m), `damage KILL unit=striker`, and then NO
# `damage KILL unit=depot` line for the rest of the run.
#
# WHY THE DEPOT LIVES, MEASURED rather than arranged: on this run-in the striker's CCIP release falls at
# t=72.0 (the same 19 km approach as attack-ccip.fbm, same 900 m, same 450 kt — and the same measured
# release tick). The CAP's briefed pickle is at t=20, when the head-on range is 24.6 km, inside Raero
# (26.9 km at this altitude) and therefore accepted; the round arrives at t=54.3. The striker is
# combat-ineffective 17.7 s before its own release point and never issues a release at all — there is no
# `sms RELEASE` line for it in the whole run. The wreck flies on and reaches the ground at t=94.0, which
# is where the run ends: that K.O. was the CAP's declared objective, so it ends the run without deciding
# it, and every still-open monitor is finalised there.
#
# WHY THE CAP ALSO DECLARES `kill unit striker`: without it the striker's loss would be nobody's declared
# objective, and the expected-loss rule would let that loss decide the run (doc/missions/verdict.md).
# With it the duel reads correctly — the striker's FAIL is the CAP's SUCCESS — and `protect` adds the
# statement `kill` cannot make: killing him AFTER the bombs were away would not have been enough. Its
# sibling escort-protect-lost.fbm is exactly that case, ONE number apart.

unit depot
  module target_soft                         # the protected: an installation, not an airframe
  team friendly
  spawn 46.90000 7.05000 ground 90.0 0

unit striker
  module f16
  team hostile
  spawn 46.90000 6.80000 900 90.0 450        # attack-ccip.fbm's run-in: 19 km out, co-track
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 60
  set datalink off
  set fcr_mode off
  set store 3 mk82
  set store 7 mk82
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode ccip
  wp 46.90000 7.05000 900 450                # the aim point IS the active steerpoint
  wp 46.95000 7.20000 3000 400               # the briefed egress beyond it

unit cap
  module f16
  team friendly
  spawn 46.90000 7.25000 900 270.0 450       # head-on, 34 km east of the striker, co-altitude
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 60
  set datalink off
  set fcr_mode acm_hud
  set fcr_range_nm 40
  set store 3 aim120
  set store 7 aim120
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set brief_release_s 20                     # <<< THE ONE NUMBER that differs from escort-protect-lost
  wp 46.90000 6.60000 900 450
  objective protect unit depot
  objective kill unit striker
  objective survive
